course: dictionary
lesson: 11188
title: Thin and light: the word wisp
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A wisp is a thin, light piece or strand of something, like a wisp of hair or a wisp of grass. Often the words around it tell you what it looks like: thin, soft and light.
explain: «Wisps of cloud float in the sky.» Float tells you the wisps drift gently, and cloud tells you what they are made of. Try your meaning in the sentence: thin, light pieces of cloud float in the sky. It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: The sentence «Cirrus are thin wisps of ice high up» explains itself. The word thin sits right next to wisps, so the context tells you a wisp is something thin. Look for these helpers before you reach for a dictionary.
fact: A wisp is a thin, light piece or strand of something, such as a wisp of hair.
fact: A wisp of smoke, cloud or steam is a thin line or small amount drifting in the air.
fact: «Wispy» is the adjective: wispy clouds are thin and light, and wispier means thinner or lighter still.
fact: Informally, a wisp of a person is a small, thin person.
fact: In science, cirrus clouds are high, thin wisps of ice.
exercise: «Wisps of smoke curl from the chimney.» What is a wisp? | A big storm | *A thin, light piece or strand | A heavy stone | A loud noise
exercise: Yanni says a wisp of a person is a giant. What does a wisp of a person mean? | A person who runs very fast | A tall, strong person | A person who sings loudly | *A small, thin person
exercise: «Clouds have names by their shape and height.» Wispy clouds high in the sky are called cirrus. What does wispy mean? | *Thin and light, like wisps | Heavy and wet | Dark and stormy | Loud and fast
test: «The wisp of hair blew across her face.» What is a wisp of hair? | A hairclip | A bald patch | A thick, heavy braid | *A thin, light strand
test: «Cirrus are thin wisps of ice high up.» Which cloud is described as thin wisps of ice high up? | stratus | *cirrus | cumulonimbus | cumulus
exam: «Stratus are flat grey sheets that may bring drizzle; cirrus are thin wisps of ice high up.» What does wisp mean in this sentence? | A puddle of melted ice | A flat grey sheet | *A thin, light strand | A heavy storm
